G6095:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at Rut.4.19; 
son of: Hezron (H2696H); 
brother of: Jerahmeel (H3396), Caleb (H3612H), Segub (H7687H) and Ashhur (H0806); 
father of: Amminadab (H5992); also called Admin (KJV: Aram) at Luk.3.33; 
§ Arni (Proper name)

G6973:
1. <b>power, lordship, sovereignty </b>, (Sophocles Tragicus), etc. 
2. <b>an oligarchy </b>, (Thucydides) 
from δῦναστεύω (ML)

G7318:
1. <b>a searching out, search </b>, (Herdotus Historicus) 
2. <b>a finding out, invention </b>, (Herdotus Historicus) 
from ἐξευρίσκω (ML)

G8009:
1. <b>adulterated, spurious, base </b>, of coin, (Theognis Elegiacus) 
2. <i>metaphorically</i> <b>base, false, spurious, fraudulent </b>, of men, (Theognis Elegiacus); of oracles, <b>deceitful </b>, (Herdotus Historicus); ἐν κιβδήλῳ (Euripides) 
from κίβδος (ML)

G8190:
1. <b>a band of robbers </b>, (Xenophon Historicus):—; <b>a retreat </b> or <b>nest of robbers </b>, (Strabo Geographus) 
2. <b>robbery </b>, in <i>plural</i>, (Lucian) 
from λῃστής (ML)

G8623:
1. <b>alternation, alternating motion </b>, τῶν σκελῶν (Plutarch) 
2. <b>a change for the worse, alteration </b>, (Plato Philosophus) 
from παραλλάσσω (ML)

G8640:
1. <b>a placing in line of battle </b>, ἐκ παρατάξεως <b>in regular battle </b>, (Thucydides), etc. 
2. of <b>marshalling </b> a political party, <b>arrangement </b>, (Aeschines Orator) 
from παρατάσσω (ML)

G8679:
1. φόνια πειρατήρια the murderous <b>ordeal </b>, (Euripides) 
2. <b>a pirate's nest </b>, (Strabo Geographus) 
from πειρα_τής (ML)

G8971:
1. <b>a stumble, trip, false step </b>, (Theognis Elegiacus) 
2. <b>a failure, misfortune, defeat </b>, (Herdotus Historicus), etc. 
from πτάξ (ML)

G20647:
1. <b>to steal clothes </b>, especially from bathers or travellers, (Plato Philosophus) 
2. generally, <b>to rob, plunder </b>, (Aristophanes Comicus) 
from λωποδύτης (ML)

G21343:
